From: QEMU Anti-Detection Patches
Date: 2025
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: Hide KVM hypervisor presence when expose_kvm is disabled

When the user sets "-cpu host,-kvm" (expose_kvm=false), also clear the
CPUID[1].ECX[31] hypervisor bit.  The existing guard only cleared
FEAT_KVM; the hypervisor bit in FEAT_1_ECX was left set from the
unconditional set in x86_cpu_load_model() or from the host passthrough
feature expansion.

Without this patch, even with "-cpu host,-kvm", CPUID[1].ECX[31] can
still advertise the hypervisor bit.

Note: Hyper-V CPUID leaves at 0x40000000 are NOT affected by this
patch.  If the user enables hv-* flags, those leaves will still be
present.  To hide them, remove hv-* flags or also disable them in
the CPU model string.

---
 target/i386/cpu.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/target/i386/cpu.c b/target/i386/cpu.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/target/i386/cpu.c
+++ b/target/i386/cpu.c
@@ -9762,6 +9762,7 @@
 
     if (!kvm_enabled() || !cpu->expose_kvm) {
         env->features[FEAT_KVM] = 0;
+        env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] &= ~CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
     }
 
     /*
